    "First Boer War"
  ],
  "explanation": "The Pretoria Peace Agreement refers specifically to the Pretoria Convention of 1881, which directly ended the First Boer War, as stated in D1S1. While D3S1 mentions other agreements also named 'Pretoria Peace Agreement' (such as the Treaty of Vereeniging in 1902), these are distinct agreements and not relevant to the war-ending role of the 1881 Pretoria Convention. The 'Second Boer War' is incorrectly attributed to the Pretoria Peace Agreement in D2S1, where it is actually the Treaty of Vereeniging that applies. Other candidates like the First Ivorian Civil War and the Second Congo War are incidental mentions and not relevant to the war-ending function of the Pretoria Peace Agreement in this context."
